              "text": "તારીખિયું — tārīkhiyũ — \"wall calendar\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "હું નવું તારીખિયું ખરીદીશ. — hũ navũ tārīkhiyũ kharīdīś — \"I will buy a new calendar.\""
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Built on તારીખ, tārīkh, date."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "તારીખિયું (tārīkhiyũ) is built on the taught tārīkh, \"date\", with the ending -iyũ. Tārīkh is a loan from Arabic tārīkh, \"a dating, a date\", through Persian; EtymDB lists the Persian word. Its Arabic root is ʾ-r-kh, \"to date a letter\" (Lane)."
            }
          ]
        },
